\section{Experiments}

\subsection{Observations and Evaluation Protocol}

The experimental log records one deterministic calculation on supplied synthetic values, rather than a named external dataset. Targets are $(-1,1,3,5,7)$, baseline predictions are $(-4,-2,0,2,4)$, and predictions after adding $3$ are $(-1,1,3,5,7)$. All five observations determine the mean residual and evaluate the three recorded settings $b=0,1.5,3$. These settings are controlled changes to one scalar within the same calculation, not independent experiments or stochastic repetitions. The slope remains fixed throughout.

There is no held-out evaluation, timing measurement, optimizer training, architecture comparison, or uncertainty estimate. The reported errors therefore describe agreement with the five observed targets only.

